# {{PROJECT_NAME}} - Ruby on Rails

> Generated: {{GENERATION_DATE}} | Claude Craft v{{VERSION}}

## What (Stack & Structure)

**Stack**: Ruby {{RUBY_VERSION}}, Rails {{RAILS_VERSION}}, Active Record, Hotwire

### Project Structure
```
app/
├── models/           # Active Record models (domain rules, validations)
│   └── concerns/     # Shared model behaviour
├── controllers/      # Thin HTTP layer (strong params, auth, rendering)
│   └── concerns/
├── services/         # Service objects (one use case = one `call`)
├── forms/            # Form objects (multi-model input)
├── queries/          # Query objects (complex reads)
├── jobs/             # Active Job (Solid Queue)
├── views/            # ERB templates + Turbo Frames/Streams
└── javascript/       # Stimulus controllers (importmap)
config/               # Routes, credentials, initializers
db/                   # Migrations, schema.rb, seeds
spec/ or test/        # RSpec or Minitest (system tests with Capybara)
```

## Why (Purpose & Organization)

### Architecture: Rails Way first, pragmatic Clean
- **Models**: persistence, validations, associations, domain rules
- **Controllers**: thin, orchestration only (strong params, authorization, response)
- **Service / Form / Query objects**: extracted only when models or controllers grow
- No mandatory hexagonal layering: follow conventions, extract on real pain

See `rules/02-architecture-ruby.md` for complete patterns.

### Critical Rules
| Rule | Reason |
|------|--------|
| `# frozen_string_literal: true` | Immutability, fewer allocations |
| RuboCop (rubocop-rails-omakase) | Code quality and consistent style |
| Strong parameters (`params.expect`) | Mass-assignment protection |
| Brakeman + bundler-audit | Security gates in CI |
| 80%+ coverage (SimpleCov) | Quality assurance |

## How (Commands & Workflows)

### Development Commands
```bash
docker compose exec app bundle install       # Install dependencies
{{CACHE_CLEAR_COMMAND}}                      # Clear cache
docker compose exec app bin/rails test       # Run tests (Minitest)
docker compose exec app bundle exec rspec    # Run tests (RSpec)
docker compose exec app bin/rubocop          # Code style
docker compose exec app bin/brakeman         # Security analysis
```

### Quality Pipeline
```bash
docker compose exec app bin/rubocop                 # Style check
docker compose exec app bin/brakeman --no-pager     # Security scan
docker compose exec app bin/bundler-audit           # Dependency CVEs
docker compose exec app bin/ci                      # Full local CI (Rails 8.1)
```

### Development Workflow
1. **Analyze** - Read code, understand domain (`rules/01-workflow-analysis.md`)
2. **TDD** - Write test -> Implement -> Refactor
3. **Quality** - Run `bin/ci` inside the container
4. **Commit** - Conventional Commits format

